<title>AUSTRALIA: HongKong Bank of Australia gets credit card.</title>
<headline>HongKong Bank of Australia gets credit card.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>HongKong Bank of Australia, a subsidiary of HSBC Holdings Plc, said on Monday it has received a licence to offer MasterCard credit cards in Australia.</p>
<p>HongKong Bank, which already offers debit card facilities, said the licence would allow it to offer a full range of card products in Australia.</p>
<p>The bank said it had reached a three-year agreement with the Commonwealth Bank of Australia to act as the card issuer and credit provider.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
